        {
          type: 'text',
          heading: '2. The Global Window Object',
          paragraphs: [
            "The global object in the browser is window. Any global variables or functions defined in your code are attached as properties of window.",
            "Through window, you access Web APIs that are separate from the core JS spec, such as the DOM (via window.document), Timers (via window.setTimeout), and Network fetches (via window.fetch)."
          ]
        },
        {
          type: 'quote',
          text: '“window is the gateway to the browser runtime stack.”'
        }
      ]
    },
    summary: 'The browser environment provides the runtime hosting JavaScript, including engine compilers (V8) and external hooks called Web APIs (the DOM, fetch, and timer bindings). Everything runs relative to the global window object.',
