          heading: '1. ECMAScript vs JavaScript',
          paragraphs: [
            "ECMAScript is the official specification managed by Ecma International. JavaScript is the programming language that implements this specification.",
            "You can think of ECMAScript as a set of blueprints, and JavaScript as the actual houses built using those blueprints by browser engines."
          ]
        },
        {
          type: 'takeaway',
          title: 'Key Takeaway',
          text: 'By standardizing JavaScript under ECMAScript, TC39 ensures that code written in 1995 remains backward-compatible, and new ESNext proposals are implemented uniformly across all modern browser engines.'
        },
        {
          type: 'text',
          heading: '2. The TC39 Proposal Process',
          paragraphs: [
            "The Technical Committee 39 (TC39) is the group of browser vendors, programmers, and academics that decides which features make it into the ECMAScript standard.",
            "New features undergo a strict 5-stage process: Stage 0 (Strawman), Stage 1 (Proposal), Stage 2 (Draft), Stage 3 (Candidate), and Stage 4 (Finished). Features in Stage 4 are scheduled for the next annual spec release."
          ]
        },
        {
          type: 'quote',
          text: '“TC39 ensures language changes are consensus-driven and backward-compatible.”'
        }
      ]
    },
    summary: 'ECMAScript (ECMA-262) governs the core syntax and behavior of JavaScript. The TC39 committee updates the standard annually using a consensus-driven 5-stage proposal framework, guaranteeing backward-compatibility across all browsers.',
    codeHtml: `<span class="code-comment">// Modern ES6+ syntax standards</span>
<span class="code-keyword">const</span> <span class="code-variable">spaceship</span> <span class="code-operator">=</span> { <span class="code-variable">name</span>: <span class="code-string">"Apollo"</span>, <span class="code-variable">speed</span>: <span class="code-number">10</span> };

<span class="code-comment">// Object destructuring proposal (Finished stage)</span>
<span class="code-keyword">const</span> { <span class="code-variable">name</span> } <span class="code-operator">=</span> <span class="code-variable">spaceship</span>;
<span class="code-variable">console</span>.<span class="code-function">log</span>(<span class="code-variable">name</span>);`,
